1
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:09,719
<i>I thought my suspicions were wrong.</i>

2
00:00:09,802 --> 00:00:11,470
But it's you!

3
00:00:11,554 --> 00:00:13,472
You fooled me!

4
00:00:13,556 --> 00:00:15,433
I love you so much, Ana.

5
00:00:15,516 --> 00:00:17,977
<i>My love for you has no lies.</i>

6
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,521
<i>I'm not saying what he did was right.</i>

7
00:00:20,604 --> 00:00:22,773
<i>But your husband truly loves you.</i>

8
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:25,317
Sometimes,
technicalities don't really matter.

9
00:00:25,401 --> 00:00:27,445
Especially if you look at the big picture.

10
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:30,281
Did he hurt you?
Did he ever hurt you physically?

11
00:00:30,364 --> 00:00:31,532
He didn't, right?

12
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:34,034
And now that you've dragged me
into all of your lies,

13
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:37,037
I need to do something to correct them.

14
00:00:37,121 --> 00:00:39,373
<i>Three bodies</i>
<i>have been recovered by the police.</i>

15
00:00:39,457 --> 00:00:42,585
<i>A relative has identified</i>
<i>the body of Brian Robles...</i>

16
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:44,670
<i>Danny Pascual,</i>

17
00:00:44,754 --> 00:00:46,255
<i>and Joel Geraldo...</i>

18
00:00:46,338 --> 00:00:47,840
We're worried about Beth.

19
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:50,259
Her siblings and I can't reach her.

20
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:52,511
Please, Beth.

21
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:55,681
Eat.

22
00:01:05,107 --> 00:01:08,110
Ben...

23
00:01:09,403 --> 00:01:10,821
Mara!

24
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:15,493
Mara!

25
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,661
Beth?

26
00:01:58,744 --> 00:01:59,995
Beth, wait.

27
00:02:00,538 --> 00:02:01,497
Beth!

28
00:02:08,045 --> 00:02:10,631
Beth! Wait!

29
00:02:11,382 --> 00:02:12,550
Beth!

30
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,178
Beth, let's talk about what happened.

31
00:02:16,262 --> 00:02:17,388
We have nothing to talk about.

32
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:18,806
No, I know you saw it.

33
00:02:18,889 --> 00:02:20,850
- Beth! Beth, wait!
- I didn't see anything!

34
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:22,434
I didn't see anything!

35
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:24,645
Beth!

36
00:02:25,521 --> 00:02:26,689
Beth!

37
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:35,507
Uh-um.

38
00:04:26,684 --> 00:04:28,435
Was the woman who died...

39
00:04:30,521 --> 00:04:31,772
your mistress?

40
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:36,652
No.

41
00:04:41,532 --> 00:04:42,741
She was family.

42
00:04:43,242 --> 00:04:44,410
Was she your relative?

43
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:47,830
Gingging and I considered her family.

44
00:04:50,165 --> 00:04:52,209
Family? Then why did you kill her?

45
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,670
You must've misunderstood
what you saw, Beth.

46
00:04:55,129 --> 00:04:56,296
It was an accident.

47
00:05:01,051 --> 00:05:03,137
My sister has a mental illness.

48
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:06,140
She didn't mean to do it.

49
00:05:13,939 --> 00:05:14,940
Beth...

50
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:20,487
are you going to tell anyone?

51
00:05:22,072 --> 00:05:24,158


52
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:29,455
Beth?

53
00:05:42,176 --> 00:05:45,888


54
00:05:45,971 --> 00:05:48,891


55
00:06:03,697 --> 00:06:05,699
- Ana?

56
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:10,037
- Come in.
W-what?

57
00:06:12,915 --> 00:06:14,083
What happened?

58
00:06:18,629 --> 00:06:19,630
Beth...

59
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:23,217

are you going to tell anyone?

60
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:29,223
Thank you.

61
00:06:33,519 --> 00:06:36,105

So, what's your plan for me here?

62
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:41,485
You'll only let me out
when it's time to feed me,

63
00:06:43,237 --> 00:06:45,072
then you'll put me back in the room?

64
00:06:46,073 --> 00:06:49,076
Is that what you do
to people who get in your way?

65
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:52,830
Are you locked up, Beth?

66
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:56,542
Are you tied up?

67
00:07:00,629 --> 00:07:02,381
Is there a gag over your mouth?

68
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:06,426
You can go home...

69
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:09,263
if you want.

70
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:14,643
You're free, Beth.

71
00:07:15,686 --> 00:07:16,770
You're free.

72
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:28,949


73
00:07:29,491 --> 00:07:31,910

But if you don't want to go home yet...

74
00:07:34,872 --> 00:07:36,540
you can use Ana's clothes.

75
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:40,210
Okay?

76
00:07:44,715 --> 00:07:46,383
Excuse me.

77
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:15,495
I recognized Brian.
He came to our house.

78
00:08:15,579 --> 00:08:18,165
And the one they couldn't identify
might be Joel.

79
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:22,085
Who's Joel?

80
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,838
Ben's sister's husband.

81
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:29,676
Oh, wow. How sordid.

82
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:34,264
Mom, is that
all you have to say? "How sordid"?

83
00:08:35,474 --> 00:08:36,642
What am I supposed to say?

84
00:08:37,643 --> 00:08:40,479
"Horrendous?" "Gruesome?"

85
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:41,647
What?

86
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:44,816
Mom, they're all connected to Ben.

87
00:08:46,568 --> 00:08:48,070
Ben knew them.

88
00:08:49,196 --> 00:08:53,283
I knew the person who died
in the next town last week.

89
00:08:53,367 --> 00:08:56,203
- Does that mean I killed them?

90
00:08:56,828 --> 00:09:00,916
Mom, the police said
the same person may have done this.

91
00:09:01,917 --> 00:09:04,002
And you think it was Ben?

92
00:09:04,086 --> 00:09:05,921
Ana, that's ridiculous!

93
00:09:06,004 --> 00:09:09,341
But Regina said Ben killed her husband.

94
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:11,593
She's crazy!

95
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:13,470
And you know what they say.

96
00:09:14,388 --> 00:09:15,305
About what?

97
00:09:15,389 --> 00:09:18,016
About people who believe a crazy person!

98
00:09:19,101 --> 00:09:21,103
- Mom.
- Ana...

99
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:25,482
Would you rather believe
Ben is a murderer?

100
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,864
What if he really is?

101
00:09:33,865 --> 00:09:35,284


102
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:42,791
Look...

103
00:09:42,874 --> 00:09:45,877
Ana, you're still in shock, okay?

104
00:09:45,961 --> 00:09:49,464
You should get some rest.

105
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:53,176
It's not good for the baby
to keep thinking about all these things.

106
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:54,678
Stop thinking.

107
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:12,321
<i>So far,</i>

108
00:10:12,404 --> 00:10:14,656
<i>three bodies have been recovered</i>
<i>by the police.</i>

109
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:18,577
<i>Relatives have identified</i>
<i>the remains of the victims.</i>

110
00:10:20,579 --> 00:10:21,913
<i>Danny Pascual...</i>

111
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:24,583
<i>Everyone will find out what you're hiding!</i>

112
00:10:27,127 --> 00:10:30,047
<i>A relative identified</i>
<i>the body of Brian Robles.</i>

113
00:10:32,215 --> 00:10:33,300
Ah!

114
00:10:34,051 --> 00:10:36,428
You want me to stop?
Is that what you said?

115
00:10:37,054 --> 00:10:39,473
Well, damn you. "Stop." Exactly.

116
00:10:39,556 --> 00:10:42,726
I've been asking you to do that.
I've asked you to stop.

117
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:44,478
I didn't want to do this either.

118
00:10:44,561 --> 00:10:46,396
That's why I'm here in Vallente, isn't it?

119
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,690
<i>Simply because I want to live in peace.</i>

120
00:10:48,774 --> 00:10:51,526
<i>The third victim</i>
<i>was identified as Joel Geraldo.</i>

121
00:10:55,155 --> 00:10:58,158
But here you are,
you damn bastard.

122
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:02,746
You all want to destroy
the things I've worked hard on.

123
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:05,457
I just want to live a quiet life
with my wife, okay?

124
00:11:22,641 --> 00:11:24,142
You look nice, Beth.

125
00:11:26,311 --> 00:11:27,396
I'll see you, Beth.

126
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:45,372
So, this is the way
to Uncle Richard's house

127
00:11:45,455 --> 00:11:47,707
from Madam Imelda's place.

128
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:51,962
Well, it's Ana's house now.
Ben bought it for her.

129
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:54,047
But does anyone live there?

130
00:11:54,131 --> 00:11:56,466
A caretaker? It doesn't look like it.

131
00:11:57,259 --> 00:11:58,927
Someone lives there.

132
00:11:59,845 --> 00:12:02,264
- Look, there's someone inside.
- Huh?

133
00:12:02,347 --> 00:12:04,433
Maybe Ben hired a caretaker.

134
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:10,814
Oh, my God.

135
00:12:14,985 --> 00:12:16,486
What the hell?

136
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,322
What's that woman doing there?

137
00:12:20,699 --> 00:12:24,536
She couldn't get inside
if she didn't know the owner, right?

138
00:12:25,412 --> 00:12:27,747
So, there really is something
between them?

139
00:12:28,582 --> 00:12:30,750
Has he moved that woman in?

140
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,145
<i>Are you sure it's them?</i>

141
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:51,563
Ask Carlos.

142
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:54,065
But why would he take Beth there?

143
00:12:55,942 --> 00:12:57,360
I don't know.

144
00:12:59,738 --> 00:13:01,573
Maybe he's trying to make you jealous

145
00:13:01,656 --> 00:13:03,241
so you'll take him back.

146
00:13:08,705 --> 00:13:10,207
I don't know.

147
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:15,545
I don't know what he's doing anymore.

148
00:13:16,296 --> 00:13:17,964
I don't know him anymore.

149
00:13:20,884 --> 00:13:22,052
Hey.

150
00:13:22,636 --> 00:13:24,721
You still haven't talked to each other?

151
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:31,436
Ana, you know
you can tell me everything, right?

152
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:34,606
Yes.

153
00:13:36,983 --> 00:13:38,068
Thank you.

154
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:39,569
Here's what we'll do.

155
00:13:39,653 --> 00:13:41,863
I'll send someone to the Bais house...

156
00:13:41,947 --> 00:13:43,907
to find out
if he's really living there

157
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:44,908
with that physical therapist.

158
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:47,160
What the hell is that?

159
00:13:47,786 --> 00:13:49,287
It was my house!

160
00:13:49,371 --> 00:13:51,998
And Ben moved that bitch in?

161
00:13:52,541 --> 00:13:53,875
Goodness!

162
00:13:53,959 --> 00:13:56,211
You're being ridiculous, Ana.

163
00:13:56,878 --> 00:13:58,380
He looked for you.

164
00:13:58,463 --> 00:13:59,714
He tried to win you back.

165
00:13:59,798 --> 00:14:01,132
But you wouldn't listen.

166
00:14:01,216 --> 00:14:05,720
Naturally, a man will find
a woman he can lean on.

167
00:14:05,804 --> 00:14:09,057
So, it's your fault
he moved that woman in.

168
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:10,600
Now it's my fault?

169
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:12,852
Who's your child here, Mom? Me or him?

170
00:14:13,395 --> 00:14:15,355
Of course you are, my dear.

171
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:17,774
I'm only thinking about
what's best for you.

172
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:21,278
Wait a second.
What's really the problem here?

173
00:14:21,361 --> 00:14:23,780
Is it because your husband
is a fake lawyer?

174
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,824
Or is it because of those bodies
that turned up,

175
00:14:25,907 --> 00:14:28,410
even though there's no evidence?
Which is it?

176
00:14:28,493 --> 00:14:31,413
Of all people,
I thought you would understand.

177
00:14:31,496 --> 00:14:33,582
Or has Ben won you over too?

178
00:14:34,416 --> 00:14:38,003
Ma, I need trust.

179
00:14:39,421 --> 00:14:41,965
I need loyalty.

180
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:44,467
You know,
all I ever hear from you

181
00:14:44,551 --> 00:14:47,137
is "I need this" or "I need that"!

182
00:14:47,804 --> 00:14:49,723
Ana, it's not just about you anymore!

183
00:14:50,599 --> 00:14:53,018
Have you even thought about
the child you're carrying?

184
00:14:53,101 --> 00:14:54,519
Have you?

185
00:14:54,603 --> 00:14:57,522
Mom, I can raise my child
even without a father.

186
00:14:58,064 --> 00:15:00,483
I don't care anymore.
I'm not going back to Ben.

187
00:15:00,567 --> 00:15:02,652
They can play house there for all I care.

188
00:15:02,736 --> 00:15:04,696
Ana, you can't just do nothing.

189
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:06,114
You need to fix this.

190
00:15:06,197 --> 00:15:08,783
You need to make this right
for your child!

191
00:15:08,867 --> 00:15:10,368
This is what's right.

192
00:15:12,996 --> 00:15:14,748
This is what's right, Mom.

193
00:15:15,415 --> 00:15:17,500
For me and my child.

194
00:16:04,756 --> 00:16:07,425
Regina, you have a visitor.

195
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:10,220
Regina.

196
00:16:12,222 --> 00:16:13,932
Regina, it's Ana.

197
00:16:15,016 --> 00:16:16,559
Do you remember me?

198
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,814
She's always like this.

199
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:24,317
She stays quiet
and doesn't talk to anyone.

200
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,572
But is she okay?

201
00:16:29,656 --> 00:16:31,449
Has she been getting sick?

202
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:33,201
She's okay.

203
00:16:33,284 --> 00:16:35,453
She eats a little.

204
00:16:35,537 --> 00:16:38,331
But she's always quiet.

205
00:16:38,415 --> 00:16:43,086
She just stares outside,
like she's waiting for someone.

206
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:47,549
Who does she say she's waiting for?

207
00:16:48,216 --> 00:16:50,760
She said she was waiting for her husband.

208
00:16:50,844 --> 00:16:54,013
He promised he'd come back for her.

209
00:17:04,941 --> 00:17:06,776
Nurse, can I take her outside?

210
00:17:08,153 --> 00:17:09,487
Just for a while.

211
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,786
She came here last night.

212
00:17:20,123 --> 00:17:21,374
Ana.

213
00:17:22,417 --> 00:17:24,252
We locked eyes.

214
00:17:24,335 --> 00:17:26,045
But she left right away.

215
00:17:30,216 --> 00:17:32,051
Ben, aren't you wondering

216
00:17:33,303 --> 00:17:34,888
why she came by?

217
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,142
Why didn't she come after me?

218
00:18:01,956 --> 00:18:03,082
Ben...

219
00:18:07,712 --> 00:18:09,047
are you using me?

220
00:18:14,427 --> 00:18:16,346
Did you want Ana to see me here,

221
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:18,598
so you could make her jealous?

222
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:20,683
Is that it, Ben?

223
00:18:31,152 --> 00:18:32,403
Last night...

224
00:18:33,363 --> 00:18:36,115
I could've left, Ben. But I didn't!

225
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:38,326
Ask me why.

226
00:18:38,993 --> 00:18:40,161
Come on, ask me.

227
00:18:41,538 --> 00:18:42,622
Because...

228
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:44,666
I'm stupid!

229
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:48,419
God, I'm so stupid!

230
00:18:48,503 --> 00:18:53,091
You have no idea what I've gone through
with you, with Ana, and this damn town!

231
00:19:08,565 --> 00:19:10,984
Ben, I actually hoped...

232
00:19:13,278 --> 00:19:16,865
I had hope
that I could replace Ana in your life.

233
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:20,827
But I was wrong.

234
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:23,580
I was wrong for thinking
that I could replace Ana in your life.

235
00:19:35,758 --> 00:19:37,427
I'm sorry, Beth.

236
00:19:45,602 --> 00:19:46,603
Ah...

237
00:19:55,069 --> 00:19:56,321
Mrs. Santos.

238
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,986
Sir, can you please open it?

239
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:15,858
This is his tattoo.

240
00:21:17,568 --> 00:21:18,945
And...

241
00:21:20,613 --> 00:21:21,864
that's his piercing.

242
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:31,499
Joel!

243
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:36,295
My husband!

244
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:42,218
I told you!
You should've taken me with you!

245
00:21:42,844 --> 00:21:46,681
Now you're gone!

246
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:52,228
Joel!

247
00:21:53,938 --> 00:21:56,024
My husband...

248
00:21:58,192 --> 00:22:01,404
You should've let me come with you...

249
00:22:05,742 --> 00:22:08,161
Joel...

250
00:22:13,124 --> 00:22:16,377
I told you he was gone.

251
00:22:18,504 --> 00:22:21,966
I told you Ben killed him.

252
00:22:23,051 --> 00:22:26,220
My husband...

253
00:23:17,855 --> 00:23:19,524
Ana, thank you.

254
00:23:20,691 --> 00:23:22,193
You made my wish come true.

255
00:23:23,528 --> 00:23:24,654
What wish?

256
00:23:26,531 --> 00:23:28,449
To find Joel.

257
00:23:31,244 --> 00:23:33,079
You're the only one who has done it.

258
00:23:35,206 --> 00:23:36,624
Not Mara,

259
00:23:37,333 --> 00:23:38,668
not my brother.

260
00:23:42,964 --> 00:23:44,465
Even though it was too late,

261
00:23:45,174 --> 00:23:47,927
what's important is that
I found my husband.

262
00:23:52,223 --> 00:23:54,976
Ma'am, time to take your medicine.

263
00:23:57,270 --> 00:23:58,771
- In just a bit.
- Okay.

264
00:24:06,654 --> 00:24:07,989
Ana, you can have this.

265
00:24:09,699 --> 00:24:12,952
Once I'm out, I'll take it back.

266
00:24:15,955 --> 00:24:17,456
Thank you, Ana.

267
00:24:18,457 --> 00:24:20,209
Focus on recovery, okay?

268
00:24:20,293 --> 00:24:22,044
Take care of yourself.

269
00:24:22,753 --> 00:24:24,172
Be safe.

270
00:24:27,633 --> 00:24:29,302
You should stay safe, Ana.

271
00:24:34,223 --> 00:24:35,975
Your husband is a monster.

272
00:24:41,689 --> 00:24:42,607
Let's go.

273
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:45,776
- Thank you, nurse.
- Thank you.

274
00:24:59,248 --> 00:25:01,626
- Thank you so much.
- Yeah, thank you also. Thank you. Okay?

275
00:25:01,709 --> 00:25:03,127
- Thanks.
- Have a nice day.

276
00:25:12,470 --> 00:25:13,971
Attorney Ben Santos.

277
00:25:15,139 --> 00:25:17,475
You need to come with us to the station.

278
00:25:21,103 --> 00:25:23,105
Is Ben already at the station?

279
00:25:23,606 --> 00:25:24,774
<i>Yes, Miss Ana.</i>

280
00:25:24,857 --> 00:25:27,360
Attorney Ben Santos is now
in our custody.

281
00:25:27,443 --> 00:25:29,820
We will take care of
your complaint against him.

282
00:25:31,781 --> 00:25:33,407
Don't hurt him.

283
00:25:33,491 --> 00:25:35,743
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>
<i>We're just going to talk to him.</i>

284
00:25:36,410 --> 00:25:37,495
<i>Bye.</i>

285
00:25:42,208 --> 00:25:45,711
This is Brian Robles, okay?

286
00:25:45,795 --> 00:25:49,507
I worked with this guy at the firm
a long time ago.

287
00:25:50,424 --> 00:25:51,592
This is Danny.

288
00:25:51,676 --> 00:25:53,803
He is a private investigator...

289
00:25:53,886 --> 00:25:55,304
who was hired by Antonio Saguil

290
00:25:55,388 --> 00:25:57,223
to do a background check on me.

291
00:25:57,682 --> 00:25:58,849
And this guy?

292
00:25:58,933 --> 00:26:00,518
That's Joel.

293
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:04,146
I don't know his last name,
but he's my sister's partner.

294
00:26:06,899 --> 00:26:08,067
Attorney.

295
00:26:08,985 --> 00:26:11,570
Isn't that too much of a coincidence?

296
00:26:11,654 --> 00:26:15,157
All of these victims are connected to you.

297
00:26:18,786 --> 00:26:19,996
What are you saying?

298
00:26:23,582 --> 00:26:28,587
Do you have anything to do
with all of this, Attorney Santos?

299
00:26:29,422 --> 00:26:31,507
Do you have evidence...

300
00:26:32,174 --> 00:26:33,259
okay?

301
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:37,346
That connects me to these murders?

302
00:26:38,389 --> 00:26:40,224
Someone saw you.

303
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:42,601
Someone tipped us off.

304
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:45,938
A tip?

305
00:26:50,901 --> 00:26:52,320
That tip?

306
00:26:53,529 --> 00:26:55,948
That is not direct evidence.

307
00:26:57,992 --> 00:27:01,579
You should know better than that,
'cause I won't take this sitting down.

308
00:27:15,843 --> 00:27:17,178
Ana?

309
00:27:22,808 --> 00:27:26,645
Gomez, this is not the first time, okay?

310
00:27:26,729 --> 00:27:29,148
That you're trying to see
if I have a motive...

311
00:27:30,024 --> 00:27:31,525
for the murders.

312
00:27:33,194 --> 00:27:35,613
Do you remember
what happened with Antonio Saguil?

313
00:27:35,696 --> 00:27:37,198
You solved that.

314
00:27:38,032 --> 00:27:40,242
It wasn't me who killed him, right?

315
00:27:41,744 --> 00:27:44,080
What could be my motive...

316
00:27:45,456 --> 00:27:47,375
to kill these people?

317
00:27:53,714 --> 00:27:55,466
I've been here for hours.

318
00:27:57,468 --> 00:27:59,220
You do not have a case against me

319
00:27:59,303 --> 00:28:00,554
because you don't have evidence.

320
00:28:00,638 --> 00:28:02,390
So, no evidence...

321
00:28:03,099 --> 00:28:04,100
no case. I go.

322
00:28:04,725 --> 00:28:07,478
Wait, Attorney.
We're not done yet.

323
00:28:07,561 --> 00:28:10,898
You're wasting
your time and your resources

324
00:28:10,981 --> 00:28:12,650
detaining me here.

325
00:28:13,192 --> 00:28:15,611
You have nothing against me.

326
00:28:15,694 --> 00:28:18,364
Or would you like me
to file a case against you?

327
00:28:21,992 --> 00:28:23,244
Thought so.

328
00:28:32,211 --> 00:28:34,713
Beth has been ignoring
my texts and calls, Ana.

329
00:28:34,797 --> 00:28:36,465
I'm worried about her.

330
00:28:39,760 --> 00:28:40,845
Hello, Kat?

331
00:28:41,303 --> 00:28:44,390
Kat, what's the update?
Is Beth still there?

332
00:28:44,473 --> 00:28:46,725
<i>Carlos and I went back to Bais.</i>

333
00:28:46,809 --> 00:28:48,644
<i>She isn't there anymore, Ana.</i>

334
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:50,563
<i>But I can go back and look again.</i>

335
00:28:50,646 --> 00:28:54,316
No, Kat. Don't do that.
Never go back to that house.

336
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:56,402
<i>Ana, you're confusing me.</i>

337
00:28:56,485 --> 00:28:58,487
<i>What exactly is going on? Tell me.</i>

338
00:28:59,488 --> 00:29:00,614
<i>Ana!</i>

339
00:29:00,698 --> 00:29:03,367
No answer.
I can't contact her anymore.

340
00:29:05,327 --> 00:29:06,912
Beth is so stubborn.

341
00:29:07,413 --> 00:29:08,664
I told her.

342
00:29:09,123 --> 00:29:11,375
I told her to stay away from you and Ben.

343
00:29:11,459 --> 00:29:13,752
But she didn't listen. She didn't stop.

344
00:29:13,836 --> 00:29:14,920
It's my fault.

345
00:29:15,004 --> 00:29:17,173
Beth might be in danger.

346
00:29:17,631 --> 00:29:18,883
In danger?

347
00:29:19,550 --> 00:29:22,386
Why?
Is Ben going to hurt my friend?

348
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:26,682
I'll go there! Where is that house?

349
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:28,726
No, Diane. You can't go there.

350
00:29:28,809 --> 00:29:32,521
I don't know what Ben is thinking.
He might hurt you too.

351
00:29:32,605 --> 00:29:35,608
I won't leave Vallente without my friend!

352
00:29:35,691 --> 00:29:37,860
We don't even know if she's still there.

353
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:40,613
Kat said she didn't see Beth there.

354
00:29:40,696 --> 00:29:43,699
So, where is she, Ana?
What happened to Beth?

355
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:46,785
I'll find out. I'm going to go there.

356
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:51,123
You just told me that Ben is dangerous.

357
00:29:51,207 --> 00:29:53,959
And you want to go alone?
No, I'm coming with you.

358
00:29:54,043 --> 00:29:55,461
Let's call the police.

359
00:29:55,544 --> 00:29:58,547
And what are we going to say?
That Beth might have been kidnapped?

360
00:29:59,215 --> 00:30:00,716
That Beth might be there?

361
00:30:01,342 --> 00:30:02,927
We have no evidence.

362
00:30:04,220 --> 00:30:06,138
What if your husband hurts you?

363
00:30:06,222 --> 00:30:08,057
I know my husband.

364
00:30:08,682 --> 00:30:11,685
If there's one person
who he will never hurt...

365
00:30:12,394 --> 00:30:13,562
it's me.

366
00:32:25,361 --> 00:32:26,445
Ben?

367
00:32:33,035 --> 00:32:34,119
Beth.

368
00:33:08,737 --> 00:33:09,905
Ana.

369
00:33:12,908 --> 00:33:14,159
You came.

370
00:33:16,286 --> 00:33:17,454
Thank you.

371
00:33:19,123 --> 00:33:20,457
I knew you'd come.

372
00:33:24,461 --> 00:33:26,255
What did you do?

373
00:33:27,965 --> 00:33:30,467
Oh. Ah, this?

374
00:33:35,764 --> 00:33:37,182
I chopped some chicken.

375
00:33:39,184 --> 00:33:40,352
I mean...

376
00:33:40,644 --> 00:33:42,730
Funny, 'cause I was thinking you'd come.

377
00:33:43,647 --> 00:33:45,232
So I'm trying to cook.

378
00:33:54,616 --> 00:33:55,701
Ana.

379
00:33:56,618 --> 00:33:58,036
I-I'll clean up.

380
00:34:03,292 --> 00:34:04,543
Sorry, Ana.

381
00:34:11,967 --> 00:34:14,720
I didn't know
you'd gotten the house cleaned up.

382
00:34:16,138 --> 00:34:18,307
Yes. Yes, Ana.

383
00:34:28,108 --> 00:34:30,444
I also had our room cleaned.

384
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:07,272
I cleaned it up for us.

385
00:35:08,941 --> 00:35:10,609
Of course, our baby.

386
00:35:18,033 --> 00:35:19,284
How are you, Ana?

387
00:35:22,371 --> 00:35:23,622
I miss you.

388
00:35:26,625 --> 00:35:29,044
Did you go to the doctor? How's our baby?

389
00:35:35,092 --> 00:35:36,760
Is this the baby's room?

390
00:35:39,012 --> 00:35:40,264
Yeah.

391
00:35:40,347 --> 00:35:41,682
It's not finished yet.

392
00:35:42,182 --> 00:35:44,017
- It's okay.
- No, Ana.

393
00:35:44,101 --> 00:35:45,602
It's supposed to be a surprise.

394
00:35:45,686 --> 00:35:46,687
I still have some work to do inside.

395
00:35:46,770 --> 00:35:48,647
- I just wanna see.
- Ana.

396
00:35:50,357 --> 00:35:51,525
Ana...

397
00:35:52,192 --> 00:35:53,861
It's messy here.

398
00:35:54,653 --> 00:35:56,655
There's paint everywhere.

399
00:35:58,991 --> 00:36:00,909
I'm painting this.

400
00:36:00,993 --> 00:36:02,661
I told you it's not ready.

401
00:36:06,582 --> 00:36:07,749
You like it?

402
00:36:07,833 --> 00:36:08,917
Yeah.

403
00:36:09,001 --> 00:36:10,669
- You wanna pick a color?
- It's nice.

404
00:36:25,142 --> 00:36:26,643
Is this Beth's?

405
00:36:31,815 --> 00:36:32,900
Yes.

406
00:36:37,070 --> 00:36:38,739
Why is there blood?

407
00:36:39,323 --> 00:36:40,407
Ben.

408
00:36:41,408 --> 00:36:42,910
What did you do?

409
00:36:45,245 --> 00:36:46,830
She's gone, Ana.

410
00:36:48,498 --> 00:36:51,335
What? Beth is gone?

411
00:36:52,252 --> 00:36:55,505
Oh, my God, Ben!
What did you do?

412
00:36:56,298 --> 00:36:59,301
Ana, she left.

413
00:37:00,719 --> 00:37:02,554
I don't believe you.

414
00:37:02,638 --> 00:37:04,139
That's the truth.

415
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:06,266
Ben, what did you do to Beth?

416
00:37:06,350 --> 00:37:07,976
Where is she?

417
00:37:08,060 --> 00:37:09,311
- Is she still here?
- Ana.

418
00:37:09,394 --> 00:37:10,938
Is she still here?

419
00:37:11,021 --> 00:37:12,898
- Where did you hide Beth?
- Ana, she already left.

420
00:37:12,981 --> 00:37:15,400
Beth! Beth!

421
00:37:17,361 --> 00:37:18,695
Beth!

422
00:37:19,780 --> 00:37:20,948
Beth?

423
00:37:22,074 --> 00:37:22,991
- Beth!
- Ana!

424
00:37:23,075 --> 00:37:25,619
- Where is she?
- Ana, she's not here anymore!

425
00:37:25,702 --> 00:37:28,038
She's gone because you killed her?

426
00:37:28,830 --> 00:37:32,501
You killed her, Ben,
just like you killed Joel.

427
00:37:35,712 --> 00:37:37,214
Oh, my God.

428
00:37:37,297 --> 00:37:39,967
Did you think I was so stupid...

429
00:37:40,050 --> 00:37:44,221
to not see the connection
of the three people you killed?

430
00:37:44,304 --> 00:37:46,306
Ben, I know!

431
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:48,308
I know you killed them

432
00:37:48,392 --> 00:37:51,144
because they found out
the secrets you were hiding!

433
00:37:52,896 --> 00:37:55,399
You've been fooling everyone.

434
00:37:55,983 --> 00:38:01,405
You've been using the cops
and bending the law to your advantage.

435
00:38:01,488 --> 00:38:04,074
How could you do it?

436
00:38:04,908 --> 00:38:08,745
You can manipulate everything, but not me!

437
00:38:09,454 --> 00:38:13,709
Not me. Not anymore. I'm done.

438
00:38:15,961 --> 00:38:17,212
What do you mean?

439
00:38:19,423 --> 00:38:21,591
I thought you came here...

440
00:38:23,260 --> 00:38:25,679
I thought you came here
because we're gonna fix things.

441
00:38:26,263 --> 00:38:27,431
No.

442
00:38:30,058 --> 00:38:32,644
There's nothing left to fix.

443
00:38:34,104 --> 00:38:35,605
We're done, Ben.

444
00:38:38,817 --> 00:38:40,819
One day,
you'll pay for what you did,

445
00:38:40,902 --> 00:38:43,572
but you won't drag me and my son
into this.

446
00:38:44,740 --> 00:38:46,575
I won't let you do it.

447
00:38:46,658 --> 00:38:48,160
Wait, Ana...

448
00:38:49,119 --> 00:38:50,537
Don't do this.

449
00:38:58,378 --> 00:38:59,629
No...

450
00:39:01,965 --> 00:39:03,133
- No...
- Stop.

451
00:39:03,216 --> 00:39:05,635
Please, let go. Please.

452
00:39:05,719 --> 00:39:08,972
Please, you can't leave me.

453
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:11,725
Ben!

454
00:39:16,146 --> 00:39:18,482
I can, and I will.

455
00:39:26,323 --> 00:39:28,825
No!

456
00:39:28,909 --> 00:39:30,035
Wake up!

457
00:39:34,623 --> 00:39:35,624
Mama!

458
00:39:42,464 --> 00:39:44,299
You really are smart.

459
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:48,220
But I'm not like you.

460
00:39:48,303 --> 00:39:52,724
Then you just have to study hard.
Do you agree?

461
00:39:52,808 --> 00:39:54,893
Fighting back, huh?

462
00:39:55,227 --> 00:39:57,729
Fight back now!

463
00:40:00,065 --> 00:40:03,485
<i>That's not the kind of life</i>
<i>I want for our child.</i>

464
00:40:04,111 --> 00:40:07,197
<i>You know how my life was before, Ben.</i>

465
00:40:08,573 --> 00:40:10,158
We will be different.

466
00:40:11,868 --> 00:40:13,703
We will be better as parents.

467
00:40:35,559 --> 00:40:37,394
No!

468
00:40:43,108 --> 00:40:44,442
Ben!

469
00:40:49,573 --> 00:40:50,615
Ben?

470
00:40:52,159 --> 00:40:53,326
No, no.

471
00:40:58,165 --> 00:41:00,083
No, no, no...

472
00:41:00,167 --> 00:41:01,376
No...

473
00:41:05,797 --> 00:41:07,048
No!

474
00:41:07,132 --> 00:41:08,466
No... Ana!

475
00:41:10,010 --> 00:41:12,095
No!

476
00:41:13,013 --> 00:41:15,265
Beth? Beth...

477
00:41:20,270 --> 00:41:21,521
Betchay?

478
00:41:26,902 --> 00:41:27,986
Beth?

479
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:33,909
Beth, it's Diane.

480
00:41:48,256 --> 00:41:49,341
Ana!

481
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:53,345
- Open up--
- Ana!

482
00:41:53,428 --> 00:41:55,222
No! Stay away from me!

483
00:41:55,305 --> 00:41:56,806
Who are you calling?

484
00:41:56,890 --> 00:41:58,266
Ana, stop!

485
00:41:58,350 --> 00:42:00,268
- Stop! Don't come closer!
- Stop!

486
00:42:33,134 --> 00:42:34,970
This is Beth's phone.

487
00:42:53,613 --> 00:42:55,282
Who are you calling?

488
00:42:55,365 --> 00:42:58,868
- No, Ben! Please!
- Who are you calling? Huh?

489
00:42:58,952 --> 00:43:01,288
- Give me your phone. Don't call anyone!
- Stop...

490
00:43:01,371 --> 00:43:03,290
Please, talk to me!

491
00:43:03,373 --> 00:43:04,541
Talk-- Ana!

492
00:43:04,624 --> 00:43:06,793
- Don't come any closer!
- Stop!

493
00:43:06,876 --> 00:43:08,920
- No! Let me go!
- Stop!

494
00:43:09,004 --> 00:43:10,046
Let me go!

495
00:43:10,130 --> 00:43:11,298
- Ana?
- Stop!

496
00:43:12,173 --> 00:43:13,508
Ana. Ana...

497
00:43:25,812 --> 00:43:27,314
Ana! Stop!

498
00:43:59,346 --> 00:44:00,597
Ben...

499
00:44:15,278 --> 00:44:16,363
Hello? Officer?

500
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:25,080
Ben! Ben!

501
00:44:25,622 --> 00:44:27,332
Ben! Ben!

502
00:44:27,415 --> 00:44:29,167
Ben, I'm sorry.

503
00:44:29,250 --> 00:44:30,877
I'm sorry. Ben...

504
00:44:31,461 --> 00:44:33,880
I'm sorry, Ben.

505
00:44:33,963 --> 00:44:35,256
Ana...

506
00:44:35,340 --> 00:44:36,508
There's... a snake.

507
00:44:41,805 --> 00:44:44,224
Oh, my God...

508
00:44:45,225 --> 00:44:47,268
Oh, my God. Ben, I'm sorry.

509
00:44:47,352 --> 00:44:50,397
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

510
00:44:50,480 --> 00:44:51,648
I'm sorry.

511
00:44:51,731 --> 00:44:52,857
I thought you were...

512
00:44:52,941 --> 00:44:54,025
- I--
- Shh.

513
00:44:54,109 --> 00:44:56,528
I didn't know.
Oh, my God, Ben.

514
00:44:56,611 --> 00:44:59,030
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

515
00:44:59,864 --> 00:45:01,324
No, Ana.

516
00:45:03,034 --> 00:45:04,285
I'm sorry.

517
00:45:06,746 --> 00:45:08,081
I'm sorry...

518
00:45:09,833 --> 00:45:11,084
I lied.

519
00:45:13,294 --> 00:45:15,547
I lied so many times.

520
00:45:18,383 --> 00:45:21,469
I'm sorry for lying to you.

521
00:45:24,472 --> 00:45:27,142
I lied because...

522
00:45:28,476 --> 00:45:31,312
I was so afraid to lose you.

523
00:45:33,231 --> 00:45:34,816
Every day,

524
00:45:35,608 --> 00:45:37,026
I fought for...

525
00:45:37,110 --> 00:45:41,531
- ...our lives and our dreams.
- No, no, no, no...

526
00:45:42,449 --> 00:45:46,035
Out of all the lies I told,

527
00:45:47,412 --> 00:45:49,080
only one thing...

528
00:45:51,833 --> 00:45:54,002
remains true.

529
00:46:00,008 --> 00:46:02,510
I love you so much.

530
00:46:07,223 --> 00:46:10,226
I love you so much.

531
00:46:14,189 --> 00:46:16,691
Please take care of our baby...

532
00:46:18,860 --> 00:46:19,944
Ben?

533
00:46:22,405 --> 00:46:24,491
Ben. Ben?

534
00:46:27,368 --> 00:46:29,370
Ben...

535
00:46:30,747 --> 00:46:32,499
No...

536
00:46:53,561 --> 00:46:54,812
Move!

537
00:46:54,896 --> 00:46:57,065
- They're inside!
- Men, move!

538
00:47:39,148 --> 00:47:40,149
Ana?

539
00:47:42,694 --> 00:47:43,820
Ana?

540
00:47:45,572 --> 00:47:48,283
Men, search the whole house!

541
00:47:48,366 --> 00:47:51,035
Please find my friend, Beth, too.

542
00:47:51,828 --> 00:47:52,954
Beth?

543
00:47:53,037 --> 00:47:55,164
Ana?

544
00:48:15,935 --> 00:48:18,938
<i>No one survives pain unchanged.</i>

545
00:48:20,315 --> 00:48:22,150
<i>When you get hurt,</i>

546
00:48:22,650 --> 00:48:24,819
<i>you change in a lot of ways.</i>

547
00:48:26,154 --> 00:48:28,239
There are some things

548
00:48:29,073 --> 00:48:31,242
that never go back
to what they used to be.

549
00:48:33,494 --> 00:48:35,163
Things that...

550
00:48:35,663 --> 00:48:39,334
you choose not to be
part of your life anymore.

551
00:48:44,547 --> 00:48:48,301
When you've gone through the most painful,

552
00:48:50,261 --> 00:48:53,681
the most difficult moment in your life,

553
00:48:55,642 --> 00:48:58,561
you have no choice but to face it.

554
00:49:01,064 --> 00:49:04,567
Sometimes, you do it
for the ones you love,

555
00:49:05,735 --> 00:49:09,155
but it should also be for yourself.

556
00:49:10,990 --> 00:49:12,825
Thanks for the treat.

557
00:49:13,409 --> 00:49:17,246
No, thank you
for taking care of my siblings.

558
00:49:17,330 --> 00:49:18,665
Oh, it's nothing.

559
00:49:18,748 --> 00:49:21,250
I'm always glad to help out.

560
00:49:22,877 --> 00:49:23,961
What's that?

561
00:49:24,045 --> 00:49:25,380
Oh, this?

562
00:49:28,007 --> 00:49:30,009
I'm planning to give it away.

563
00:49:31,052 --> 00:49:33,054
I won't get to use it anyway.

564
00:49:39,727 --> 00:49:41,896
To help you forget about them?

565
00:49:44,232 --> 00:49:45,483
I guess so.

566
00:49:48,486 --> 00:49:51,739
You've had a tough time in Vallente.

567
00:49:52,198 --> 00:49:54,283
Especially with what Ben did to you.

568
00:49:55,493 --> 00:49:57,328
What exactly happened?

569
00:49:59,664 --> 00:50:03,292
I don't know.
I was out of my mind back there.

570
00:50:04,711 --> 00:50:08,464
What's important is it's all over.
You've moved on.

571
00:50:08,548 --> 00:50:12,427
And finally,
you've opened up your own clinic.

572
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:14,971
Yes, finally!

573
00:50:15,888 --> 00:50:19,308
I'm glad you found a business partner too.

574
00:50:19,392 --> 00:50:21,227
I hope I get to know them.

575
00:50:21,728 --> 00:50:24,230
Oh, yeah, they're almost here.

576
00:50:25,773 --> 00:50:26,774
Oh!

577
00:50:28,651 --> 00:50:30,403
Hi, Beth. Sorry I'm late.

578
00:50:30,486 --> 00:50:32,989
- Traffic was so bad.
- It's okay. This is Diane.

579
00:50:33,573 --> 00:50:34,824
- My friend.
- Hi, Diane.

580
00:50:34,907 --> 00:50:37,076
I'm Attorney De Castro.

581
00:50:37,160 --> 00:50:38,828
Hello, Attorney.

582
00:50:39,245 --> 00:50:41,497
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.

583
00:50:44,667 --> 00:50:46,252
So, um...

584
00:50:47,879 --> 00:50:49,130
when do we start?

585
00:50:50,798 --> 00:50:53,801
<i>Pain changes how you see things.</i>

586
00:50:57,764 --> 00:50:58,765
Juancho?

587
00:50:58,848 --> 00:51:00,224
Auntie!

588
00:51:01,392 --> 00:51:02,727
Son!

589
00:51:03,853 --> 00:51:05,021
Hi, Ma!

590
00:51:06,731 --> 00:51:08,649
<i>It shows...</i>

591
00:51:09,442 --> 00:51:11,527
<i>what's really important.</i>

592
00:51:12,278 --> 00:51:14,781
<i>And what you can survive</i>

593
00:51:15,406 --> 00:51:17,158
<i>in the name of love.</i>

594
00:51:19,535 --> 00:51:21,704
<i>That's my experience</i>

595
00:51:22,371 --> 00:51:26,542
<i>as a designer, a daughter,</i>

596
00:51:27,460 --> 00:51:28,795
<i>a wife,</i>

597
00:51:30,171 --> 00:51:32,590
<i>and as a person.</i>

598
00:51:32,673 --> 00:51:35,343
Dear residents of Vallente,

599
00:51:35,426 --> 00:51:39,263
our Child of Visayas 2031,

600
00:51:39,347 --> 00:51:41,933
Ana Madrigal-Santos!

601
00:51:46,854 --> 00:51:49,148
And presenting the award

602
00:51:49,232 --> 00:51:51,692
is our very own...

603
00:51:51,776 --> 00:51:55,446
Mayor Benjamin Santos!

604
00:52:13,965 --> 00:52:16,217
- Thank you, son.
- You're welcome.

605
00:52:27,645 --> 00:52:28,646
Thank you.

606
00:52:28,729 --> 00:52:31,899
I am so proud of you, stranger.

607
00:52:36,112 --> 00:52:39,115
Smile.

608
00:52:57,842 --> 00:53:00,052
<i>The opening of the new law firm...</i>

609
00:53:00,136 --> 00:53:02,847
<i>- ...coincides with the news of the opening</i>

610
00:53:02,930 --> 00:53:06,726
<i>of his new business venture,</i>
<i>a physical therapy clinic.</i>

611
00:53:06,809 --> 00:53:08,436
<i>More details soon.</i>

612
00:53:09,061 --> 00:53:10,062
Hello?

613
00:53:10,730 --> 00:53:12,106
<i>Hello, Ma'am Ana.</i>

614
00:53:13,357 --> 00:53:15,443
- Yes?
- <i>We have a new client</i>

615
00:53:15,526 --> 00:53:19,238
<i>requesting a gown for the opening</i>
<i>of her physical therapy clinic.</i>

616
00:53:19,947 --> 00:53:23,117
<i>She insists that you accommodate her.</i>

617
00:53:24,619 --> 00:53:26,621
And she is...

618
00:53:26,913 --> 00:53:29,248
<i>Elizabeth Valdez.</i>

619
00:53:33,461 --> 00:53:34,795
Papa?

620
00:53:36,923 --> 00:53:38,341
Papa?

621
00:53:57,985 --> 00:53:59,153
Elijah?

622
00:54:10,456 --> 00:54:11,874
Elijah?

623
00:54:13,834 --> 00:54:15,086
Mama!

624
00:54:16,128 --> 00:54:17,463
Oh...

625
00:54:18,756 --> 00:54:20,007
Baby.

626
00:54:21,092 --> 00:54:23,344
What happened, dear?

627
00:54:23,427 --> 00:54:25,346
Why are you up at this hour?

628
00:54:25,429 --> 00:54:29,684
I had a dream that Papa went outside.

629
00:54:33,312 --> 00:54:35,982
- Mama!
- Oh! Oh...

630
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:38,943
Mm. Baby.

631
00:54:39,026 --> 00:54:41,570
I'm scared, Mama.

632
00:54:42,947 --> 00:54:44,365
It's okay.

633
00:54:45,950 --> 00:54:47,201
He'll be back.

634
00:56:31,764 --> 00:56:33,516
<i>As the mother of La Familia,</i>

635
00:56:33,599 --> 00:56:36,352
I make sure
that whenever we make a decision,

636
00:56:36,435 --> 00:56:38,771
<i>we always put the company first,</i>

637
00:56:38,854 --> 00:56:42,274
<i>especially our safety standards.</i>

638
00:56:44,235 --> 00:56:46,445
I am La Familia.

639
00:56:46,529 --> 00:56:48,572
<i>- I won't let you ruin this company.</i>

640
00:56:48,656 --> 00:56:52,368
<i>That's cruel!</i>
<i>That's why your family left!</i>

641
00:56:52,451 --> 00:56:55,704
Karma will catch up to you!

642
00:56:55,788 --> 00:56:58,290
That's just karma. I am Diana Aragon.

643
00:56:58,374 --> 00:57:00,960
Miss D, something went wrong
at the feeding program.

644
00:57:01,043 --> 00:57:03,712
Does anybody know what caused this?

645
00:57:03,796 --> 00:57:04,880
Give me answers!

646
00:57:04,964 --> 00:57:06,966
- Miss D! Miss D!
- Miss D!

647
00:57:10,636 --> 00:57:12,805
<i>I just know that someday,</i>

648
00:57:12,888 --> 00:57:14,306
<i>you'll be the main star.</i>

649
00:57:14,390 --> 00:57:16,892
<i>It's your birthday.</i>

650
00:57:16,976 --> 00:57:18,602
It's okay, Ma.

651
00:57:18,686 --> 00:57:20,688
<i>You know</i>
<i>I don't like celebrating anyway, right?</i>

652
00:57:20,771 --> 00:57:21,772
What's wrong?

653
00:57:21,856 --> 00:57:23,482
Your dad ran off with all our money.

654
00:57:23,566 --> 00:57:25,568
- How much was it?
- About a million.

655
00:57:28,988 --> 00:57:33,159
<i>According to our sources,</i>
<i>Ms. Aragon has an only daughter.</i>

656
00:57:33,242 --> 00:57:35,536
She's so lucky then!
Must be the heir to the fortune.

657
00:57:35,619 --> 00:57:37,663
What they need to see is authenticity.

658
00:57:37,746 --> 00:57:41,083
<i>And trust me,</i>
<i>your family is very, very marketable.</i>

659
00:57:44,086 --> 00:57:47,131
The first day
of the only daughter at La Familia.

660
00:57:47,214 --> 00:57:48,674
- Good morning, Miss D.
- Miss D?

661
00:57:48,757 --> 00:57:51,802
Your family
is still the only one you can trust.

662
00:57:51,886 --> 00:57:55,723
Where is this family now as we talk?

663
00:57:55,806 --> 00:57:57,266
I choose my daughter.

664
00:57:57,349 --> 00:57:59,268
And I chose to understand her too.

665
00:57:59,351 --> 00:58:02,771
Saving Diana means saving La Familia.

666
00:58:02,855 --> 00:58:04,315
What are we supposed to do about all this?

667
00:58:04,398 --> 00:58:05,858
She's not looking for a real daughter.

668
00:58:05,941 --> 00:58:10,279
A doll. A doll she can dress up
and make do whatever she wants.

669
00:58:10,362 --> 00:58:12,656
You ruined our relationship.

670
00:58:12,740 --> 00:58:14,408
Patricia is like this

671
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:17,411
because you always made her feel
like she was never enough.

672
00:58:17,494 --> 00:58:21,624
You're surrounded by beautiful things,
but we all know you're all alone.

673
00:58:21,707 --> 00:58:22,958
- Enough!
- Stop!

674
00:58:23,042 --> 00:58:26,420
I thought something changed,
but nothing has.

675
00:58:26,503 --> 00:58:28,214
<i>You just have to give her a chance.</i>

676
00:58:28,297 --> 00:58:30,382
- She's not a bad person.
- Only to you.

677
00:58:30,466 --> 00:58:31,967
<i>What kind of daughter are you?</i>

678
00:58:32,051 --> 00:58:34,803
<i>Before asking me</i>
<i>what kind of daughter I am,</i>

679
00:58:34,887 --> 00:58:36,972
ask yourself what kind of mother she is.

680
00:58:37,056 --> 00:58:38,807
Is that really how you see me?

681
00:58:39,308 --> 00:58:40,726
<i>All I know is...</i>

682
00:58:40,809 --> 00:58:45,439
you'd do anything
and sacrifice everything for La Familia.

683
00:58:45,522 --> 00:58:49,401
I'm facing you as a human,
so show me some respect.

684
00:58:49,818 --> 00:58:54,573
Then stop acting like this is
the biggest inconvenience of your life.

685
00:58:54,657 --> 00:58:55,783
Hey!
